// C primitive: `T?` in a type position, and before a case as in
// `Int?.absent`, is sugar for the enum that applies @optional, specialized
// with T, and `for … in` unwraps the payload of its one payload case. Where
// `T?` is expected, a value of T is promoted to that case holding it, as in
// Swift: `return 5` from a function returning `Int?`, an argument, an
// assignment, and either side of `=`. A new binding names the case,
// `let x: Int?.present(5)`; `Int?(5)` is not Range, since an enum value is
// always a case. Absence is the absent case, `.absent`; there is no nil
// literal. C resolves all of these; it never names the type or its cases.
@builtin
macro optional(): Enum
